# LangChain ADLC Workshop — Environment Variables
#
#   cp .env.example .env      # then fill in the values below
#   uv run python verify_setup.py   # confirms the labs can run
#
# Two model access paths are supported. You only need ONE.
#   PATH 1 — Direct API key (default): set OPENAI_API_KEY, leave OPENAI_BASE_URL unset.
#   PATH 2 — LangSmith LLM Gateway:    set LANGSMITH_GATEWAY + LANGSMITH_GATEWAY_API_KEY,
#                                      and comment OPENAI_API_KEY out entirely.
# the README (Model access section) explains how each path works and how to tell which one is active.
#
# Note: the labs load this file WITHOUT override, so anything exported in your shell
# wins over what is written here.

# =============================================================================
# WHO YOU ARE (fill this in first if you are in a shared workspace)
# =============================================================================
# Datasets, annotation queues and tracing projects are workspace-global. In a workshop where
# everyone shares one LangSmith workspace, all 15 people would seed the SAME dataset and read each
# other's traces. Set your initials here and every artifact you create is suffixed with them:
#   vendor-due-diligence-eval-tr, langchain-adlc-workshop-tr, dd-agent-baseline-tr, …
# Leave it blank for a solo run and nothing is renamed.
PARTICIPANT=

# =============================================================================
# PATH 1: Direct API key (default — uncomment and fill in)
# =============================================================================
# When you set OPENAI_API_KEY (or ANTHROPIC_API_KEY) and do NOT set OPENAI_BASE_URL
# or ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL, the labs use the provider's API directly.
#
# The model layer (day1/src/models.py) treats the gateway as configured when LANGSMITH_GATEWAY is
# set, or when OPENAI_BASE_URL / ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL points at gateway.smith.langchain.com. With
# none of those set it takes the direct provider path. `verify_setup.py` prints which one you are on.

# OpenAI (default)
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-your-openai-key
# Anthropic (workshop-provided — uncomment to use)
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-your-anthropic-key
# Model tiers (see the rationale + measurements at the top of day1/src/models.py).
# Defaults: agent=openai:gpt-4.1-mini  heavy=openai:gpt-4.1  judge=openai:gpt-5.4
# Override the agent tier and the judge tier independently:
# LABS_MODEL=openai:gpt-4.1-mini
# LABS_JUDGE_MODEL=openai:gpt-5.4

# Default base URL (optional — leave blank for the provider's default)
# When set, this is used for the provider's API endpoint. When blank, the provider's
# default is used (e.g., https://api.openai.com for OpenAI).
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://api.anthropic.com

# =============================================================================
# PATH 2: LangSmith LLM Gateway (uncomment to use)
# =============================================================================
# On this path your app holds NO provider key. It authenticates to the gateway with a LangSmith
# key, and the gateway uses the workspace's stored Provider Secret to reach OpenAI. Comment
# OPENAI_API_KEY out above — if the labs still work, you have proved the provider credential is
# no longer in your app.
#
# Prerequisites (one-time, by a workspace admin — see the README (Model access section)):
#   - LLM Gateway enabled for the organization
#   - Provider Secret set in Settings -> Workspace -> Integrations -> Provider Secrets
#   - A workspace-scoped key whose role has the `gateway:invoke` permission
#
# LANGSMITH_GATEWAY=true
# LANGSMITH_GATEWAY_API_KEY=lsv2_sk_your_service_key
#
# LANGSMITH_GATEWAY=true is the documented switch, and routes every supported chat model through
# https://gateway.smith.langchain.com. For a regional instance, set the URL instead of `true`:
# LANGSMITH_GATEWAY=https://eu.gateway.smith.langchain.com
#
# Older/equivalent form — still supported, and what you need if you want to route ONE provider to
# the gateway and leave the rest alone. A provider BASE_URL takes precedence over the switch above:
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://gateway.smith.langchain.com/openai
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://gateway.smith.langchain.com/anthropic
#
# Two things worth knowing before you pick a variable name:
#
# 1. LANGSMITH_GATEWAY_API_KEY is the name the official docs use, and the one to prefer.
#    models.py also accepts LANGSMITH_API_KEY_GATEWAY (the same four words, two of them
#    transposed — a spelling in circulation elsewhere) and LC_GATEWAY_KEY, so an existing .env
#    keeps working. Do not go hunting for the difference; every spelling above is read.
# 2. Do NOT reuse LANGSMITH_API_KEY for this. `langgraph deploy` strips that reserved variable
#    during upload, so a deployed agent loses its gateway credential and fails at runtime with an
#    auth error while working perfectly on your laptop. A PAT there is a last-resort local
#    fallback only.

# =============================================================================
# LangSmith tracing
# =============================================================================
LANGSMITH_TRACING=true
LANGSMITH_API_KEY=lsv2_pt_your-langsmith-pat   # tracing (and PAT fallback for the gateway)
LANGSMITH_PROJECT=langchain-adlc-workshop
LANGSMITH_WORKSPACE_ID=your-workspace-uuid

# --- LangSmith UI base (override for self-hosted) ---
# LANGSMITH_UI_BASE=https://smith.langchain.com

# =============================================================================
# Optional services
# =============================================================================
# These are OPTIONAL — the labs work without them. They add extra capabilities.

# --- Live web research (optional) ---
# When set, the agent can search the live web for vendors not in the bundled data.
# When unset, the agent uses only the bundled synthetic vendor database.
# Get a key at https://tavily.com/
# TAVILY_API_KEY=tvly-your-tavily-key

# --- OpenSanctions API for live sanctions screening (optional) ---
# When set, the screen_vendor tool calls the OpenSanctions /match API in addition to the local
# synthetic sanctions list. When unset, only the local list is used (offline-safe).
# Free for non-commercial use (CC BY-NC 4.0). Sign up at https://www.opensanctions.org/account/
# OPENSANCTIONS_API_KEY=your-opensanctions-key
